---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Hackathon Win | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="How I turned 50+ scattered PM requirements into a simple agentic experience that won Best Use of AI and shipped into production across Microsoft."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--violet">
    <div class="container container--narrow">

      <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back">← Back</a>

      <span class="tag">AI Product · Hackathon · Microsoft</span>
      <h1>From hackathon win to org-wide deployment</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I replaced a 50+ requirement wiki and a cumbersome form with a single agentic experience
        connected to Azure DevOps. It won Best Use of AI, shipped into production, and became a
        catalyst for how PMs across the org work today.
      </p>

      <div class="outcomes-strip">
        <div class="outcome"><span class="outcome__num">1st</span><span class="outcome__label">Best Use of AI, Microsoft hackathon</span></div>
        <div class="outcome"><span class="outcome__num">100s</span><span class="outcome__label">of users with access post-adoption</span></div>
        <div class="outcome"><span class="outcome__num">Shipped</span><span class="outcome__label">into production, built upon by others</span></div>
      </div>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>
        Every PM on our team had to navigate the same friction every time they created new work:
        find the right requirements across a 50+ item wiki, fill out a cumbersome form manually,
        then create and assign tasks in Azure DevOps by hand. The process was slow, inconsistent,
        and relied entirely on each PM knowing where to look and what to fill in.
      </p>
      <p>
        The information existed. The tools existed. Nobody had connected them.
      </p>

      <h2>My role</h2>
      <p>
        I designed and built the solution during a Microsoft hackathon. The constraint was the
        hackathon timeframe. The goal was something that actually worked, not a demo.
      </p>

      <h2>What I built</h2>
      <p>
        A simple agentic experience that replaced the entire manual process. The agent:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Analyzes the PRD to understand the product context</li>
        <li>Asks the PM targeted questions to gather requirements, release stage, and dependencies</li>
        <li>Creates and assigns tasks in Azure DevOps automatically, based on its analysis and the PM's answers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The interaction model was a conversation, not a form. The PM describes their product;
        the agent figures out the rest. No wiki to search, no fields to fill, no manual task creation.
      </p>

      <h2>The outcome</h2>
      <p>
        It won Best Use of AI at the Microsoft hackathon, and then it shipped. That distinction
        matters: most hackathon projects are prototypes. This one was adopted at the highest
        organizational level, with hundreds of people getting access to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        More importantly, it didn't just get used. It got built upon. Other teams extended it,
        added to it, connected it to other workflows. It became one of many agents in a broader
        ecosystem, but it was one of the first and it kicked off the shift. The way PMs in our
        org use agents today traces back to this project.
      </p>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <div class="nav-row">
        <a href={`${base}/work/ai-design-repo`} class="btn btn--ghost">← Previous: AI Design Repo</a>
        <a href={`${base}/work/org-ai-initiatives`} class="btn">Next: Org AI initiatives →</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: var(--space-12); }
  .back { display: inline-block; font-size: var(--size-sm); font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text-muted); text-decoration: none; margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .tag { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); display: inline-block; }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--size-xl); color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-12); max-width: 58ch; }
  .outcomes-strip { display: flex; gap: var(--space-12); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .outcome { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); }
  .outcome__num { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--size-4xl); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-accent); line-height: 1; }
  .outcome__label { font-size: var(--size-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: none; }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--space-12); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .btn { display: inline-block; font-size: var(--size-sm); font-weight: 600; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-accent); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.15s; }
  .btn:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); color: #fff; }
  .btn--ghost { background: transparent; color: var(--color-accent); border: 1.5px solid var(--color-accent); }
  .btn--ghost:hover { background: var(--color-tag-bg); color: var(--color-accent-hover); }
  .nav-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-4); }
</style>
